WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.240
"Hey! What are you doing?!

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:02.120
"A sequel."

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:03.820
"I... don't understand"

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:04.680
"Yeah, me neither.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.220
We pretty much nailed it the first time."

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.300
Hello Internet, welcome to--

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:08.920
*BZZZT*

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.760
Hey boys... want to play some volleyball?

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.180
"Gross! Does all inter-dimensional TV have to rely on juvenile violence?"

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.540
"Well, Summer, maybe people that create things aren't concerned with your delicate sensibilities."

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:22.640
*Farting noises*

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:28.320
(Gravity falls theme song)

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.720
(Film Theory Intro)

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:48.260
Hello Internet, welcome to FILM THEORY!

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.000
(Matpat &amp; Rick): "GGRAAAAASSSS"

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.420
"Tastes bad-aaah."

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.940
Since the beginning of this channel

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.200
THE SINGLE most requested series you've asked me to cover

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.460
has been Gravity Falls.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:02.600
At the time, I'd never heard of it, but based on your recommendations Steph and I started watching it

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:06.200
and instantly we had found ourselves a new favorite show.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.700
Hilarious characters,

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.060
fantastic story lines,

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:09.940
hidden codes,

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.240
and secret conspiracies,

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:13.620
all while brother and sister Dipper and Mabel Pines

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:15.740
solve mysteries around Gravity Falls, Oregon?

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.840
It was like a dream come true!

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.160
But from a theory perspective we had come too late.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:21.620
By the time this channel started,

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:24.240
the biggest mystery of the series had been solved and confirmed.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.960
The final few episodes were just about to air.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:26.960
And sure,

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.680
I had some thoughts about how Weirdmageddon came to an abrupt close

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:34.920
and how it didn't really end the series since you can't erase memories and then have them magically come back

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.600
without the main antagonist Bill Cipher also somehow still being alive.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.880
But with the show wrapped there just wasn't a whole lot to say.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:45.040
All I had left was... a hole... in my life

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:48.280
a hole aching for another smart animated series.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:51.380
Well, that's not a hundred percent true; I was left with a hole in my life and a

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:52.560
"GRAPPLING HOOK!"

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.200
Enter Rick and Morty;

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.120
it had everything I had loved about Gravity Falls

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.000
It was smart, the characters were endearing

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.000
There was even a sense of underlying mystery to be  solved

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.300
The only difference was that it was just a *bit* more mature.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.020
"I'm gonna need you to take these seeds into the bathroom,

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:09.940
and I'm gonna need you to put 'em WAAAY up inside your butthole, Morty."

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:10.660
"In my butt?"

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:11.800
Or should I say immature?

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.960
At the time, I didn't suspect that there could ever

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.200
be a deeper reason why these two series

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.600
resonated with me so strongly.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.240
I never suspected that the mastermind behind Gravity Falls

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.240
just so happened to be good friends with Rick and Morty's creator

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.060
Justin Roiland.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.000
And I absolutely would never have expected

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.500
that the two had created shows that not only shared the same universe,

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.340
or more accurately, MULTIVERSE,

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:33.260
but had made it so that Rick and Morty

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:36.120
is the secret sequel to Gravity Falls

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.660
You heard that right, Rick and Morty is the unofficial

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:40.920
season three of Gravity Falls;

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.600
a story directly connected to and happening

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.100
around and after Weirdmageddon.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.100
So, pull out your journals and prepare to get

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.600
schwifty as we nerd out over the biggest mystery these two

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.140
amazing shows could have thrown our way.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.680
Now, the idea that the two shows are connected in some way

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.100
has been around for a while.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.100
In episode ten of season one of Rick and Morty,

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.100
"Close Encounters of the Rick Kind",

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.440
there's a teeny tiny easter egg

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.860
that started people speculating.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:08.600
As Rick tries to escape getting captured by the Council of Ricks -

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.840
which is a governing body of different versions of himself collected across

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.940
other parallel realities, duh -

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:16.460
he creates numerous portals to throw off his pursuers,

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.640
each leading to a different universe.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:21.100
And you can watch this episode a hundred times

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.380
and still miss the Gravity Falls connection.

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:27.180
Through one of those portals flies a pen, a notebook,

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.620
and a coffee cup with a question mark on it.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:34.200
The question mark is immediately a dead giveaway that this is connected to Gravity Falls in some way,

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:38.200
considering it's the logo for that show's main setting, the Mystery Shack™,

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.200
but we can do it one better.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:45.220
We can trace to the exact moment that these items fly through the portal in the first place.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:48.160
In the Gravity Falls episode "Society of the Blind Eye",

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.480
we see Mabel and Dipper's great uncle Stan

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.720
working to rebuild a transdimensional portal

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:54.720
in his secret basement laboratory.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:58.720
When he fires it up, the suction of the portal causes him to lose three items.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.620
A pen, a notebook,

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:04.340
and, you guessed it, a coffee cup with the signature question mark on it.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:07.820
-- the exact three items that we see fly though Rick's portal.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:10.980
So, very early in "Rick and Mortynight's Run",

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:15.000
you have yourselves proof positive that these two shows share a universe.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.600
Or should I say one of an infinite number of possible universes?

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:20.860
SCREW THE MUMBO JUMBO! Let's just say it plain and simple:

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.960
They're connected and very intentionally so.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:24.700
But here's the thing:

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.700
this is where most websites quote unquote

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.700
"Proving" this theory STOP.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.700
One easter egg. Done. Confirmed.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.180
Way to dig deep there, guys.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:34.700
Watch out, we got some heavy lore researchers over here.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:36.960
[mocking imitation]
"Heavy. Lore. Researchers.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:40.620
Only... o-only the hardest hitting investigative journalism here, guys.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:42.620
But, you know what? Don't leave an underpaid,

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:45.100
freelance blogger to do a theorist's job, my friends,

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:48.240
because there is so, SO much more to this theory.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:51.060
For instance, in the episode "Big Trouble in Little Sanchez",

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:55.860
the B-story has Jerry and Beth going to marriage counseling on the planet Nuptia-4.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:58.360
As the two begin their therapy, in the background on the monitor

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:04.540
is an odd depiction of some sort of weird pyramid with a tall hat and a single eyeball.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:09.460
The iconic design of Gravity Falls' greatest villain: Bill Cipher

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.580
And when I say Gravity Falls' greatest villain...

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.760
for all you Rick and Morty fans who've never seen the show

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:15.040
lemme give you some context.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:16.340
BILL: You deserve a prize!

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:16.840
Here!

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:18.580
Have a head that's always screaming!

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:23.300
Matpat: This guy is so powerful and SO evil...

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.820
he burned his entire original dimension

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:29.060
killing off everyone in it, including  his family, friends, and parents.

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:33.300
So, for the good people of Nuptia-4 to be analyzing Bill Cipher in some way...

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:37.900
it's both fascinating and potentially troubling for the entire Rick and Morty universe.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:41.400
To have a threat like that lurking around in the background, it could spell disaster

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.740
for everyone that we know and love in this world.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:47.700
Multi-worlds. Multiverse. Just assume that it's always a multiverse.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.000
But to truly see how these connections flesh out,

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.880
you've got to be really hardcore.

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:56.100
You've got to be ready for some deep lore, off platform codebreaking.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:57.320
YOU'VE GOT TO

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:59.260
-dramatic pause-

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:00.460
read a book.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:04.800
In the Gravity Falls book, the canon copy of the show's Journal #3,

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:07.280
which is the most important item from that series,

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:10.020
which they published in full and released,

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:12.940
the connection between these two franchises is not only unavoidable,

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:16.300
but also starts to have implications for both show's stories,

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:20.520
explaining why all of this is so much more than just a series of fun easter eggs.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:26.360
So, Journal #3 documents Stanford Pines's research into the odd things happening around Gravity Falls, Oregon,

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:31.820
but it also tells of his time spent exploring other dimensions and the creatures he uncovers during his journeys,

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:32.640
and yet,

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:36.080
the text that you see on every page is only half the story.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:39.140
This book is a puzzle-solver's dream, because

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:42.600
on practically every single page of the journal is a coded message

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:44.880
and the codes vary throughout the book;

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:48.760
*Caesar Ciphers, where you substitute the original letter for the third letter that came before it.
*(@matpat learn to spell)

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.860
Atbash Ciphers, where you decode the text by reversing the letters.

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:56.080
Vigenère Ciphers, where each letter shift depends on some hidden key word.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:59.760
And there's more. There is so much more in this thing

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:05.440
and what you'll find is that certain codes are related to certain characters leaving notes throughout the journal.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:09.600
For instance, Ford, the author of the journal, has a specific symbol code.

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:13.200
Every time you decipher one of these pages you can know that it's him talking.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:19.020
And wouldn't you know it, but Bill Cipher, old pyramid head over here, also has his own set of codes in the book.

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:21.420
Specifically, substituting symbols for letters.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:23.420
Most of the time, he's threatening the characters.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:27.220
For instance, on the page about Ford himself, Bill's message translates to:

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:31.740
"BIRTHDAY JUNE FIFTEENTH 
DEATHDAY SOONER THAN YOU THINK"

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:37.580
Greeeeat. So, an all powerful god creature with a murder complex and propensity for stove pipe hats is

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:42.700
not only reading my diary, but adding cute little notes in the margins about my impending doom.

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:48.420
And just because this feels like the appropriate time to mention it, remember this was a show that ran on a Disney channel

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:53.560
and while all the codes and messages are fun and interesting and contain little easter egg references to the main series,

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:55.560
there's one in particular that stands out.

00:07:55.560 --> 00:08:00.080
Ford recounts that for 30 years he traveled the multiverse to determine how to defeat Bill,

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.380
engaging in many different daring adventures,

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:06.720
but in the process, he becomes an outlaw across multiple different dimensions,

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:10.800
stealing supplies for his quantum destabilizer, the weapon that he planned

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.800
would defeat Bill once and for all.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:15.240
He even shows us a copy of his wanted poster in the journal,

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:18.620
but here's the thing: in the corner of that wanted poster

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:20.820
is a another code from Bill Cipher.

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:23.400
A code that, when translated, says,

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:25.260
"RICK WAS HERE"

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:27.440
Wait, what? Rick who?

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:31.000
In the entire Gravity Falls series, there is no character named Rick,

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:35.780
but could it be referring to "Rick" Rick? "Rick Sanchez" Rick? "Rick and Morty" Rick?

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:39.400
"Lovable Genius Drunk" Rick? "The Ultimate SzeChuan Sauce Fan" Rick?

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:44.340
But for that to be the case, that would mean that Bill Cipher somehow knew about Rick,

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:50.660
that there's some connection with the journal and Stanford and Rick Sanchez, and Rick and Morty and this unified theory of odd.

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:55.140
So spurred on by this random phrase, I kept digging through the book

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:58.220
and what I found was shocking.

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:00.960
While recounting his adventures, Ford mentions that he quote,

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:07.040
"Traveled with bandits, learned to speak 13 languages," and even got caught in a fistfight with a talking couch [he means chair]. End quote.

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:11.800
That caught my attention, because in "Rick and Morty", we've seen that dimension.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:14.800
Again, in the episode "Close Rickcounters with the Rick Kind",

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:16.800
we see the furniture dimension,

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:22.940
a world like our own, but where the couches and chairs are alive and people are the things that are used to be sat upon.

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:26.700
So, if Ford got in a fight with a talking couch somewhere in the multiverse,

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:29.060
it probably would have been here.

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:31.260
But, the references keep going.

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:35.300
Earlier in Journal #3, there is two pages filled with creature silhouettes,

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:38.680
as Ford draws out the strange things he's encountered and can't explain.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.400
And while most of them show up in episodes of Gravity Falls,

00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:45.480
there's also a handful that are directly from the adventures of Rick.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:50.220
Hidden among those silhouettes is a Zigerion, the con artist aliens from "M. Night Shaym-Aliens!";

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:54.280
there's also the giant silhouette of Cthulhu - and not just any Cthulhu,

00:09:54.280 --> 00:10:00.060
but one that looks oddly similar to the one appearing in the opening sequence of every episode of Rick and Morty,

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:02.260
and let's not forget, there's also a plumbus.

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:05.640
Just a regular old plumbus, complete with proper Fleeb rubbing.

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:09.000
I mean, everyone has a Plumbus in their home, so it shouldn't be that much of a surprise.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:09.700
But it's HERE!

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:14.960
All here in Ford's book, showing us that he's come across all these things from Rick and Morty.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.040
But what does this all mean?

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:18.740
Well, remember how Ford said that he ran with a team of bandits?

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:21.240
And how his Wanted poster said "RICK WAS HERE"?

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:26.720
This all seems to imply that Ford was a fourth known member of Rick's gang of international outlaws,

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:31.600
along with Birdperson, and Squanchy, and that Ford's quest to piece together the Quantum Destabilizer

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:36.700
by stealing items from across the Multiverse is part of the reason why Rick and his gang are wanted men!

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:41.600
I mean just like Rick, Ford also eventually hides amongst his family for cover.

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:45.180
It's also why Bill Cipher would be the one to leave that message.

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:48.660
Bill must know of Rick because he has a history with Stanford,

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:54.500
and was following the comings and goings of a group of people trying to piece together a weapon that was meant to KILL him.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:56.480
And if all of this wasn't mindblowing enough,

00:10:56.480 --> 00:11:02.560
we also know that most of Rick and Morty is happening AFTER Gravity Falls' Weirdmageddon series finale.

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:04.740
AND that Bill Cipher is still a threat!

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:09.420
Journal #3 ends with Stanford writing about the events depicted in the final episodes of the series:

00:11:09.420 --> 00:11:12.460
defeating Bill, travelling the world with his estranged brother,

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:16.900
but Bill is STILL leaving threatening notes in the background.

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:21.220
Meaning that he, too, survived and is probably eager to have his revenge.

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:23.560
HOLY poopybutthole, Rick and Morty fans,

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:26.680
that would be why he was being analysed in Nuptia-4.

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:32.020
It also means that there is a very real, very canon possibility of Rick and Ford crossing paths again;

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:36.160
joining up one last time to fight the returning threat of Bill Cipher.

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:39.400
And if you think that none of this would happen, that they're still just easter eggs,

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:43.080
the ties between the shows are just getting stronger and more frequent.

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:46.500
In the SzeChuan-drenched April Fool's launch of Rick and Morty season three,

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:51.520
we not only see Dipper and Mabel versions of Morty in the background of the Council of Ricks,

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:56.480
but we also see a physical copy of Journal #3 in Morty's hands.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:12:00.100
In practically the same frame as you see Mabel and Dipper in the background,

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:03.340
you can see the reinforced edges of a maroon journal.

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:04.780
And the hints just keep showing up.

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:08.760
During Rick and Morty's season two break, you can check out the galactic federation prison

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:12.260
where Rick was being detained on the official Rickstaverse Instagram.

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:15.820
Just like a "Where's Waldo?", if you scout those pages, you'll find --

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:16.840
[DRAMATIC PAUSE FOR EFFECT]

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:19.200
-- a plumbus. Just a regular old plumbus.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:26.120
But near his personal effects, you can actually see the Stan mug, pen, and pad lying on the table.

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:30.240
So obviously canonically the evidence is there, and a crossover SHOULD happen.

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:34.260
But a lot of times rights issues and things like that make it impossible.

00:12:34.260 --> 00:12:37.120
But at the very least, as Rick and Morty season three continues,

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:39.980
Hopefully there are at least a few more easter eggs to chew on.

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:44.560
And if nothing else, simply knowing that two of the greatest scientific minds in fiction

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:50.560
were off having adventures together is a pretty darn incredible thing for all of us fans of both series.

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:53.560
And thaaaat's the way the news goes!

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:54.480
*buuurps*
[Gross, MatPat]

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:58.080
But hey, remember, that's just a theory!

00:12:58.080 --> 00:12:59.380
A FILM -- !

00:12:59.380 --> 00:12:59.880
*BOOM B*ITCH*

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:00.380
[MatPat's dead cALL THE POLICE]

